[{:db/id 17592186068680 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a92ecba4-785f-5234-a5b9-74e110a01066"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a92ecba4-785f-5234-a5b9-74e110a01066" :question/id #uuid "a92ecba4-785f-5234-a5b9-74e110a01066" :question/math-academy-id "q-167515" :question/problem "Find the expression for the length $a(x)$ in terms of $x.$\n\n$a(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the right triangle formed by two sides and a diagonal.\n\n![](images/ba/ba2ba6039f294df10db14d592ecc03f301a483745dfab2758a8fdc7df8a2b7d8.png)\n\nAccording to the Pythagorean theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+6)^{2} & ={x}^{2}+{a}^{2} \\\\ {a}^{2} & =(x+6)^{2}-{x}^{2} \\\\ a & =\\sqrt{(x+6)^{2}-{x}^{2}} \\\\ a & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+12x+36-{x}^{2}} \\\\ a & =\\sqrt{12x+36} \\\\ a & =\\sqrt{4(3x+9)} \\\\ a & =\\sqrt{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{3x+9} \\\\ a & =2\\sqrt{3x+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9166490f-e949-5c2b-b086-c9c3c85b54de"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9166490f-e949-5c2b-b086-c9c3c85b54de" :answer-field/id #uuid "9166490f-e949-5c2b-b086-c9c3c85b54de" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-a1e14b9e-7fe9-592e-bd7b-579eb12ef45f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a1e14b9e-7fe9-592e-bd7b-579eb12ef45f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1e14b9e-7fe9-592e-bd7b-579eb12ef45f" :answer/id #uuid "a1e14b9e-7fe9-592e-bd7b-579eb12ef45f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{12x+36}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129142 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-152957b4-dc54-5769-bd44-bd7dec40a548"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-152957b4-dc54-5769-bd44-bd7dec40a548" :question/id #uuid "152957b4-dc54-5769-bd44-bd7dec40a548" :question/math-academy-id "q-167516" :question/problem "![](images/46/4692bd00e1ba3f3db0d09da40ae2d85cf908c304185846c5dd0247ac6a2411c5.png)\n\nUsing the fact that the area of the piece of land is $108$ square feet, it can be shown that the value of $x$ is given by one of the roots of the polynomial\n\n$$\np(x)={x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-972.\n$$\n\nWhich of the above diagrams could be the graph of $y=p(x)?$ Enter \"A\", \"B\", \"C\", or \"D\" (without quotes).\n\nThe diagram which shows $y=p(x)$ is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze the given polynomial:\n\n$$\np(x)={x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-972\n$$\n\nThe degree ($n=3$) is odd, and the leading coefficient (${a}_{3}=1$) is positive. Therefore, the polynomial has the following end behavior:\n\n* $p(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty .$\n\n* $p(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$ \n\nOnly the graph $A$ satisfies these conditions." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-61e2bf24-a108-5cef-9f88-dbe1fef86fa5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-61e2bf24-a108-5cef-9f88-dbe1fef86fa5" :answer-field/id #uuid "61e2bf24-a108-5cef-9f88-dbe1fef86fa5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b9a2ddbe-25aa-5681-9077-7c169747b5f9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b9a2ddbe-25aa-5681-9077-7c169747b5f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b9a2ddbe-25aa-5681-9077-7c169747b5f9" :answer/id #uuid "b9a2ddbe-25aa-5681-9077-7c169747b5f9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087755 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-def0feb0-2a39-52c6-9068-aa1b2c2978c9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-def0feb0-2a39-52c6-9068-aa1b2c2978c9" :question/id #uuid "def0feb0-2a39-52c6-9068-aa1b2c2978c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-167517" :question/problem "Determine which of $x=6$, $x=9,$ and $x=10$ is a root of $p(x),$ and use this information to write down a factor of $p(x)$ in the form $(x-r).$\n\n{{field-1}}is a factor of $p(x)$" :question/worked-solution "The factor theorem states that $(x-r)$ is a factor of a polynomial $p(x)$ if and only if the root $x=r$ is also a root of $p(x).$ \n\nHere, we consider the numbers $6$, $9,$ and $10$ as possible roots. Let's check each of these values in turn.\n\n* $x=6$ is not a root of $p(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(6) & =(6)^{3}+3(6)^{2}-972 \\\\  & =216+108-972 \\\\  & =-648 \\\\  & \\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n* $x=9$ is a root of $p(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(9) & =(9)^{3}+3(9)^{2}-972 \\\\  & =729+243-972 \\\\  & =972-972 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n* $x=10$ is not a root of $p(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(10) & =(10)^{3}+3(10)^{2}-972 \\\\  & =1\\,000+300-972 \\\\  & =328 \\\\  & \\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the factor theorem, $(x-9)$ is a factor of $p(x).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-13985908-0030-5395-bdf1-39d1d4146009"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-13985908-0030-5395-bdf1-39d1d4146009" :answer-field/id #uuid "13985908-0030-5395-bdf1-39d1d4146009" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-a4d56bde-124f-56bb-ab0f-be7499671792" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a4d56bde-124f-56bb-ab0f-be7499671792"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4d56bde-124f-56bb-ab0f-be7499671792" :answer/id #uuid "a4d56bde-124f-56bb-ab0f-be7499671792" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-9)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133825 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f871500c-ae9a-570c-8801-41a03ea03c76"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f871500c-ae9a-570c-8801-41a03ea03c76" :question/id #uuid "f871500c-ae9a-570c-8801-41a03ea03c76" :question/math-academy-id "q-167518" :question/problem "The polynomial $p(x)$ can be factored as \n\n$$\np(x)=(x-9)\\cdot q(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x)$ is a quadratic polynomial. Find $q(x).$\n\n$q(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To factor $p(x),$ we need to find its other factors.\n\nBecause $(x-9)$ is a factor of $p(x),$ we know that $(x-9)$ divides $p(x)$ with no remainder. So, to begin factoring $p(x),$ we can divide it by $(x-9)$ using synthetic division:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $9$ | $1$ | $3$ | $0$ | $-972$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $9$ | $108$ | $972$ |\n|  | $1$ | $12$ | $108$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-972}{x-9}=({x}^{2}+12x+108),\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-972=(x-9)({x}^{2}+12x+108).\n$$\n\nTo see whether the quadratic polynomial ${x}^{2}+12x+108$ can be factored any further, we calculate its discriminant:\n\n$$\n{b}^{2}-4ac={12}^{2}-4(1)(108)=-288<0\n$$\n\nSo, the quadratic polynomial ${x}^{2}+12x+108$ cannot be factored over the real numbers since its discriminant is negative. \n\nTherefore, the full factorization of $p(x)$ over the real numbers is given by \n\n$$\n(x-9)({x}^{2}+12x+108).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b03df3ec-0172-5e69-a59d-f8dd469d4012"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b03df3ec-0172-5e69-a59d-f8dd469d4012" :answer-field/id #uuid "b03df3ec-0172-5e69-a59d-f8dd469d4012" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-9102a43a-cdf1-5e62-84ba-e119681ed4cd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9102a43a-cdf1-5e62-84ba-e119681ed4cd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9102a43a-cdf1-5e62-84ba-e119681ed4cd" :answer/id #uuid "9102a43a-cdf1-5e62-84ba-e119681ed4cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x^2+12x+108" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087830 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-18714db5-7435-5dc3-be40-cc8ecbd5c18b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-18714db5-7435-5dc3-be40-cc8ecbd5c18b" :question/id #uuid "18714db5-7435-5dc3-be40-cc8ecbd5c18b" :question/math-academy-id "q-167519" :question/problem "The equation ${x}^{2}+12x+108=0$ can be written in the form $(x+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $p+q$, and solve the equation.\n\n$p+q\\,=$\n{{field-1}}\n$,\\,x=-6\\,\\pm \\,\\text{i}$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "We first move the constant to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+12x+108 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+12x & =-108\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+12x & =-108 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2\\cdot 6x+{6}^{2}-{6}^{2} & =-108 \\\\ (x+6)^{2}-36 & =-108 \\\\ (x+6)^{2} & =-72\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=6,q=-72,$ and $p+q=-66.$\n\nFinally, we solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+6)^{2} & =-72 \\\\ x+6 & =\\pm \\sqrt{-72} \\\\ x+6 & =\\pm \\sqrt{-36\\cdot 2} \\\\ x+6 & =\\pm 6\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{i} \\\\ x & =-6\\pm \\text{i}\\,6\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has two solutions, $x=-6+6\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{i}$ and $x=-6-6\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{i}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-93fafb0c-e45e-5efb-b68e-b2094c3fa0f5" "answer-field-03dd5854-cdae-544b-93a0-890bf29fb831"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-93fafb0c-e45e-5efb-b68e-b2094c3fa0f5" :answer-field/id #uuid "93fafb0c-e45e-5efb-b68e-b2094c3fa0f5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-4dfecd9e-e348-57b6-b46e-61f3cff328c6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4dfecd9e-e348-57b6-b46e-61f3cff328c6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4dfecd9e-e348-57b6-b46e-61f3cff328c6" :answer/id #uuid "4dfecd9e-e348-57b6-b46e-61f3cff328c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-66" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-03dd5854-cdae-544b-93a0-890bf29fb831" :answer-field/id #uuid "03dd5854-cdae-544b-93a0-890bf29fb831" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-12ce6eac-149a-5a2a-b5dd-6ca034848a11" :answer-field/choices ["answer-12ce6eac-149a-5a2a-b5dd-6ca034848a11"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12ce6eac-149a-5a2a-b5dd-6ca034848a11" :answer/id #uuid "12ce6eac-149a-5a2a-b5dd-6ca034848a11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054735 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3a956a31-5964-5931-a8c8-e6aacda5b4d2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-3a956a31-5964-5931-a8c8-e6aacda5b4d2" :question/id #uuid "3a956a31-5964-5931-a8c8-e6aacda5b4d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-167520" :question/problem "The magnitude of the complex numbers found in part $5$ equals{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's pick the complex number $z=-6+6\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{i}.$\n\nFor a complex number $z=a+b\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFor the complex number $z=-6+6\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{i},$ we have $a=-6$ and $b=6\\sqrt{2}.$ So, the magnitude is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}|-6+6\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{i}| & =\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+(6\\sqrt{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{6}^{2}\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}\\cdot 3} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5b844ac2-2039-543b-8af3-0016295b91da"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5b844ac2-2039-543b-8af3-0016295b91da" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b844ac2-2039-543b-8af3-0016295b91da" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-4e704852-6515-506a-bd4c-9aa898a46290" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4e704852-6515-506a-bd4c-9aa898a46290"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e704852-6515-506a-bd4c-9aa898a46290" :answer/id #uuid "4e704852-6515-506a-bd4c-9aa898a46290" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "multistep-9c965847-fddb-50a9-8bf6-395ed4b6617e" :multistep/id #uuid "9c965847-fddb-50a9-8bf6-395ed4b6617e" :multistep/context "![](images/7a/7a8bc1c792d05f95436cddb344874ba544f3b28d9f11d30a4f7bbd380846d4ce.png)\n\nMatt wants to build a chicken coop on a rectangular piece of land. The diagonal has a length of $x+6,$ one side of the rectangle has a length of $x,$ and the second side has a length of $a(x).$" :multistep/steps ["step-3be99005-17dc-5a40-acd0-b07dcde789c3" "step-fa5d68c6-bc7c-5272-b2bf-5bdba68775cb" "step-93f96480-3463-5547-801b-b3e19c4f8877" "step-5d8fbef6-550a-5de4-b86a-b63e2109cff5" "step-1b55fecf-97c1-588b-8abb-dad1dd24e478" "step-3f70b7ff-0c39-5208-8d2c-11f1125a600b"] :multistep/first-step "step-3be99005-17dc-5a40-acd0-b07dcde789c3" :db/ensure [:multistep/validate]} {:db/id "step-3be99005-17dc-5a40-acd0-b07dcde789c3" :step/id #uuid "3be99005-17dc-5a40-acd0-b07dcde789c3" :step/content "question-a92ecba4-785f-5234-a5b9-74e110a01066" :step/next "step-fa5d68c6-bc7c-5272-b2bf-5bdba68775cb" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-fa5d68c6-bc7c-5272-b2bf-5bdba68775cb" :step/id #uuid "fa5d68c6-bc7c-5272-b2bf-5bdba68775cb" :step/content "question-152957b4-dc54-5769-bd44-bd7dec40a548" :step/next "step-93f96480-3463-5547-801b-b3e19c4f8877" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-93f96480-3463-5547-801b-b3e19c4f8877" :step/id #uuid "93f96480-3463-5547-801b-b3e19c4f8877" :step/content "question-def0feb0-2a39-52c6-9068-aa1b2c2978c9" :step/next "step-5d8fbef6-550a-5de4-b86a-b63e2109cff5" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-5d8fbef6-550a-5de4-b86a-b63e2109cff5" :step/id #uuid "5d8fbef6-550a-5de4-b86a-b63e2109cff5" :step/content "question-f871500c-ae9a-570c-8801-41a03ea03c76" :step/next "step-1b55fecf-97c1-588b-8abb-dad1dd24e478" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-1b55fecf-97c1-588b-8abb-dad1dd24e478" :step/id #uuid "1b55fecf-97c1-588b-8abb-dad1dd24e478" :step/content "question-18714db5-7435-5dc3-be40-cc8ecbd5c18b" :step/next "step-3f70b7ff-0c39-5208-8d2c-11f1125a600b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-3f70b7ff-0c39-5208-8d2c-11f1125a600b" :step/id #uuid "3f70b7ff-0c39-5208-8d2c-11f1125a600b" :step/content "question-3a956a31-5964-5931-a8c8-e6aacda5b4d2" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "assigned-problem-e424c9c6-6ee7-55cc-ad7e-4f961ce5f753" :assigned-problem/id #uuid "e424c9c6-6ee7-55cc-ad7e-4f961ce5f753" :assigned-problem/content "multistep-9c965847-fddb-50a9-8bf6-395ed4b6617e" :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [17592186049224 17592186050046 17592186049242 17592186048497 17592186049695 17592186049831] :db/ensure [:assigned-problem/validate]} {:db/id "activity-58d0f926-5ac2-5b19-a1e9-133e114a3342" :activity/id #uuid "58d0f926-5ac2-5b19-a1e9-133e114a3342" :activity/title "Radical Functions and Polynomials in Geometrical Settings" :activity/type :activity.type/assignment :activity/steps ["step-62dc4bbb-8f96-5d57-9536-27bda4344483"] :activity/first-step "step-62dc4bbb-8f96-5d57-9536-27bda4344483" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-62dc4bbb-8f96-5d57-9536-27bda4344483" :step/id #uuid "62dc4bbb-8f96-5d57-9536-27bda4344483" :step/content "assigned-problem-e424c9c6-6ee7-55cc-ad7e-4f961ce5f753" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188319 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b70ed03e-6463-5d38-ae5e-1f3dea3b3eb8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b70ed03e-6463-5d38-ae5e-1f3dea3b3eb8" :question/id #uuid "b70ed03e-6463-5d38-ae5e-1f3dea3b3eb8" :question/math-academy-id "q-104053" :question/problem "![](images/b8/b8131b2ca68e378ef96c1b57e655db0a89d6e5207f0ac842612c64b30a963912.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-2,5].$ The graph of ${f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above, where the areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $1,$ $2$ and $5,$ respectively (from left to right). Find the maximum value of $f(x)$ on the interval $[-2,5]$ given that $f(1)=-12.$" :question/worked-solution "According to the candidates test, the maximum value of $f(x)$ on $[-2,5]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval.\n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points:\n\nWe see that ${f}^{′}(x)$ is defined everywhere on $x\\in (-2,5),$ and ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ at $x=\\pm 1.$ Therefore, the candidates are  $x=-2,-1,1,5.$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the value of $f$ for each candidate using the fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\nUsing the given information and the fundamental theorem of calculus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =-12 \\\\ f(-1) & =f(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{-1}{f}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =f(1)-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{f}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-12-(-2) \\\\  & =-12+2 \\\\  & =-10 \\\\ f(-2) & =f(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{-2}{f}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =f(1)-{\\int }_{-2}^{1}{f}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-12-(-2+1) \\\\  & =-12+1 \\\\  & =-11 \\\\ f(5) & =f(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{5}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-12-5 \\\\  & =-17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Select the largest value of $f$ from our candidates.\n\nComparing the values of $f$ found in step $2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{max}}=max\\{-12,-10,-11,-17\\}=-10.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the maximum value of $f$ is  ${f}_{\\text{max}}=-10,$ and the value of $x$ that maximizes $f(x)$ is ${x}_{\\text{max}}=-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-94b92d65-4457-5e1c-8c99-2be1b9018bda"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-94b92d65-4457-5e1c-8c99-2be1b9018bda" :answer-field/id #uuid "94b92d65-4457-5e1c-8c99-2be1b9018bda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c0474143-18b2-5d56-a3ca-e652dce65abe" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c0474143-18b2-5d56-a3ca-e652dce65abe" "answer-079ed11e-518b-573c-aa01-ad6a596181cb" "answer-b64dbb57-aa2e-57ce-8ba1-baf93f0d0a51" "answer-be43a691-2e56-56b2-9c4c-68d6f001fcb5" "answer-1bb43d11-d981-5b1d-a441-dc7bb7487b09"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c0474143-18b2-5d56-a3ca-e652dce65abe" :answer/id #uuid "c0474143-18b2-5d56-a3ca-e652dce65abe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-079ed11e-518b-573c-aa01-ad6a596181cb" :answer/id #uuid "079ed11e-518b-573c-aa01-ad6a596181cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b64dbb57-aa2e-57ce-8ba1-baf93f0d0a51" :answer/id #uuid "b64dbb57-aa2e-57ce-8ba1-baf93f0d0a51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be43a691-2e56-56b2-9c4c-68d6f001fcb5" :answer/id #uuid "be43a691-2e56-56b2-9c4c-68d6f001fcb5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1bb43d11-d981-5b1d-a441-dc7bb7487b09" :answer/id #uuid "1bb43d11-d981-5b1d-a441-dc7bb7487b09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188584 :question/problem "![](images/9d/9d3726847858c1afc66497820a48fa6d6bbe39e4d909b84b562a2daeea085bb4.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-3,3].$ The graph of ${f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above. Find the maximum value of $f(x)$ on the interval $[-3,3]$ given that $f(-1)=2.$" :question/worked-solution "According to the candidates test, the maximum value of $f(x)$ on $[-3,3]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval. \n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points:\n\nWe see that ${f}^{′}(x)$ is defined everywhere on $x\\in (-3,3),$ and ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ at $x=-2.$ Therefore, the candidates are $x=-3,-2,3.$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the value of $f$ for each candidate using the fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\nThe function comprises $2$ triangles, $2$ rectangles, and $1$ trapezoid. Let's add the areas bounded by these shapes to our diagram:\n\n![](images/99/99f558b3c1d86c5638543361a63823f13a9e01f2cc5042d0f781080f9f33c8a2.png)\n\nUsing the given information and the fundamental theorem of calculus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) & =2 \\\\ f(-2) & =f(-1)+{\\int }_{-1}^{-2}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =f(-1)-{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1 \\\\ f(-3) & =f(-1)+{\\int }_{-1}^{-3}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =f(-1)-{\\int }_{-3}^{-1}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2-(-\\frac{3}{2}+1) \\\\  & =2-(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ f(3) & =f(-1)+{\\int }_{-1}^{3}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2+2+4+\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Select the largest value of $f$ from our candidates. \n\nComparing the values of $f$ found in step $2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{max}}=max\\{1,\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{19}{2}\\}=\\frac{19}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the maximum value of $f$ is ${f}_{\\text{max}}=\\frac{19}{2},$ and the value of $x$ that maximizes $f(x)$ is ${x}_{\\text{max}}=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186185784 :answer-field/correct 17592186185786 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188318 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-69626226-2183-5bc4-b118-9ee330e48ca6" "question-2c6e54a6-aeaf-5247-9068-bf68741c13b9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-69626226-2183-5bc4-b118-9ee330e48ca6" :question/id #uuid "69626226-2183-5bc4-b118-9ee330e48ca6" :question/math-academy-id "q-344169" :question/problem "![](images/3a/3a971f2e8581ad9a623a8c8541ee1fcae5911fa0d3ae1b91923d19612d74ec9c.png)\n\nThe function $s(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-7,-1].$ The graph of ${s}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $s(x),$ is shown above, where the area of the region between the graph and the $x$-axis is $14.$\n\nGiven that $s(-1)=3,$ what is the minimum value ${s}_{\\text{min}}$ of $s(x)$ on the interval $[-7,-1]?$\n\n${s}_{\\text{min}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "According to the candidates test, the minimum value of $s(x)$ on $[-7,-1]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval.\n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points:\n\nWe see that ${s}^{′}(x)$ is defined everywhere on $x\\in (-7,-1),$ and ${s}^{′}(x)\\ne 0$ inside the interval. Therefore, the candidates are $x=-7,-1.$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the value of $s$ for each candidate using the fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\nUsing the given information and the fundamental theorem of calculus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s(-1) & =3 \\\\ s(-7) & =s(-1)+{\\int }_{-1}^{-7}{s}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =s(-1)-{\\int }_{-7}^{-1}{s}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3-(-14) \\\\  & =17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Select the smallest value of $s$ from our candidates.\n\nComparing the values of $s$ found in step $2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{s}_{\\text{min}}=min\\{17,3\\}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of $s$ is ${s}_{\\text{min}}=3,$ and the value of $x$ that minimizes $s(x)$ is ${x}_{\\text{min}}=-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c0d9913c-f4ac-5073-baaf-6eb787330138"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c0d9913c-f4ac-5073-baaf-6eb787330138" :answer-field/id #uuid "c0d9913c-f4ac-5073-baaf-6eb787330138" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-cae9fb4d-e189-5423-8d13-3a85f24bfe76" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cae9fb4d-e189-5423-8d13-3a85f24bfe76"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cae9fb4d-e189-5423-8d13-3a85f24bfe76" :answer/id #uuid "cae9fb4d-e189-5423-8d13-3a85f24bfe76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2c6e54a6-aeaf-5247-9068-bf68741c13b9" :question/id #uuid "2c6e54a6-aeaf-5247-9068-bf68741c13b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-344177" :question/problem "![](images/75/7571f7cb43a21a8369fc9b8197c25788a4005242d373aba2ffce44e7f6221cd6.png)\n\nThe function $g(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-6,2].$ The graph of ${g}^{′}(x)$, the derivative of $g(x),$ is shown above, where the areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $8$ and $3,$ respectively (from left to right).\n\nGiven that $g(2)=4,$ what is the minimum value ${g}_{\\text{min}}$ of $g(x)$ on the interval $[-6,2]?$\n\n${g}_{\\text{min}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "According to the candidates test, the minimum value of $g(x)$ on $[-6,2]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval.\n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points:\n\nWe see that ${g}^{′}(x)$ is defined everywhere on $x\\in (-6,2),$ and ${g}^{′}(x)=0$ at $x=-1.$ Therefore, the candidates are $x=-6,-1,2.$\n\n**Step 2**:  Compute the value of $g$ for each candidate using the fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\nUsing the given information and the fundamental theorem of calculus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(2) & =4 \\\\ g(-1) & =g(2)+{\\int }_{2}^{-1}{g}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =g(2)-{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{g}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4-(-3) \\\\  & =7 \\\\ g(-6) & =g(2)+{\\int }_{2}^{-6}{g}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =g(2)-{\\int }_{-6}^{2}{g}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4-(8+(-3)) \\\\  & =4-5 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Select the smallest value of $g$ from our candidates.\n\nComparing the values of $g$ found in step $2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{g}_{\\text{min}}=min\\{4,7,-1\\}=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of $g$ is ${g}_{\\text{min}}=-1,$ and the value of $x$ that minimizes $g(x)$ is ${x}_{\\text{min}}=-6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-64590d23-2a3d-57b0-ad84-82063765d606"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-64590d23-2a3d-57b0-ad84-82063765d606" :answer-field/id #uuid "64590d23-2a3d-57b0-ad84-82063765d606" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b3f13395-bb5b-5cb7-9ee3-5858a0482aea" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b3f13395-bb5b-5cb7-9ee3-5858a0482aea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3f13395-bb5b-5cb7-9ee3-5858a0482aea" :answer/id #uuid "b3f13395-bb5b-5cb7-9ee3-5858a0482aea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188320 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bfdcc57a-5fbc-57f0-b88e-30c636d05052"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-bfdcc57a-5fbc-57f0-b88e-30c636d05052" :question/id #uuid "bfdcc57a-5fbc-57f0-b88e-30c636d05052" :question/math-academy-id "q-344468" :question/problem "![](images/36/36a84f32380e5735b130f6b8fce26655738a0c86b210a732893dc8500d9cbbf8.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-4,5].$ The graph of ${f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above. Given that $f(2)=-3,$ what is the minimum value ${f}_{\\text{min}}$ of $f(x)$ on the interval $[-4,5]?$\n\n${f}_{\\text{min}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "According to the candidates test, the minimum value of $f(x)$ on $[-4,5]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval. \n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points:\n\nWe see that ${f}^{′}(x)$ is defined everywhere on $x\\in (-4,5),$ and ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ at $x=2.$ Therefore, the candidates are $x=-4,2,5.$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the value of $f$ for each candidate using the fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\nThe function is made up of $2$ trapezoids. Let's add the areas bounded by these shapes to our diagram:\n\n![](images/cf/cf8e3aa5a6000966c44b36071b2269540578cf123a19024a20a62fb61896dc51.png)\n\nUsing the given information and the fundamental theorem of calculus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) & =-3 \\\\ f(-4) & =f(2)+{\\int }_{2}^{-4}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =f(2)-{\\int }_{-4}^{2}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3-(-16) \\\\  & =13 \\\\ f(5) & =f(2)+{\\int }_{2}^{5}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3+4 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Select the smallest value of $f$ from our candidates. \n\nComparing the values of $f$ found in step $2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{min}}=min\\{-3,13,1\\}=-3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of $f$ is ${f}_{\\text{min}}=-3,$ and the value of $x$ that minimizes $f(x)$ is ${x}_{\\text{min}}=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0a41a06a-2eac-576e-969d-bc422a8f4058"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0a41a06a-2eac-576e-969d-bc422a8f4058" :answer-field/id #uuid "0a41a06a-2eac-576e-969d-bc422a8f4058" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-9e9434cb-bb9c-5324-9bf4-b108c900c3b0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9e9434cb-bb9c-5324-9bf4-b108c900c3b0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9e9434cb-bb9c-5324-9bf4-b108c900c3b0" :answer/id #uuid "9e9434cb-bb9c-5324-9bf4-b108c900c3b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-5870eef6-66a6-5267-a4c5-8d6d376b114f" :activity/id #uuid "5870eef6-66a6-5267-a4c5-8d6d376b114f" :activity/title "Further Optimizing Functions Using Graphs of Derivatives" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049623 :activity/course 17592186046669 :activity/steps ["step-d4e316e6-be69-5a8b-9bfa-15c379ef577c" "step-ee64bc37-0183-5fdf-9406-c969e1bd6184" "step-e9bbfa59-99fe-599d-bb21-d9652af49793" "step-34f4e575-17c0-53d6-bf0b-41cef82d3ff6" "step-b34474a6-a092-595e-81ba-f0cf9597bd95"] :activity/first-step "step-d4e316e6-be69-5a8b-9bfa-15c379ef577c" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-d4e316e6-be69-5a8b-9bfa-15c379ef577c" :step/id #uuid "d4e316e6-be69-5a8b-9bfa-15c379ef577c" :step/content "question-b70ed03e-6463-5d38-ae5e-1f3dea3b3eb8" :step/next "step-ee64bc37-0183-5fdf-9406-c969e1bd6184" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-ee64bc37-0183-5fdf-9406-c969e1bd6184" :step/id #uuid "ee64bc37-0183-5fdf-9406-c969e1bd6184" :step/content 17592186188584 :step/next "step-e9bbfa59-99fe-599d-bb21-d9652af49793" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-e9bbfa59-99fe-599d-bb21-d9652af49793" :step/id #uuid "e9bbfa59-99fe-599d-bb21-d9652af49793" :step/content "question-69626226-2183-5bc4-b118-9ee330e48ca6" :step/next "step-34f4e575-17c0-53d6-bf0b-41cef82d3ff6" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-34f4e575-17c0-53d6-bf0b-41cef82d3ff6" :step/id #uuid "34f4e575-17c0-53d6-bf0b-41cef82d3ff6" :step/content "question-2c6e54a6-aeaf-5247-9068-bf68741c13b9" :step/next "step-b34474a6-a092-595e-81ba-f0cf9597bd95" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-b34474a6-a092-595e-81ba-f0cf9597bd95" :step/id #uuid "b34474a6-a092-595e-81ba-f0cf9597bd95" :step/content "question-bfdcc57a-5fbc-57f0-b88e-30c636d05052" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078537 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-986f7504-f85e-51dd-a6eb-fbd91caed65d" "question-a0ff3000-90f6-50f0-b55e-baca4a2294a7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078249 :question/problem "Find $\\sin{\\theta},$ $\\cos{\\theta},$ and $\\tan{\\theta}$ for the triangle below.\n\n![](images/ed/ed11931671711d754241c84981e7cebf12f04bdae56a1c8b26a194a6bf44b7ca.png)" :question/worked-solution "Remember the acronym \"SOH-CAH-TOA.\"\n\n- The sine of an angle is equal to the opposite divided by the hypotenuse (S-O-H). Relative to the angle $\\theta,$ the opposite side is $\\overline{AC},$ and the hypotenuse is $\\overline{BC}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\sin{\\theta} = \\dfrac{AC}{BC} = \\dfrac{3}{5}.\n$$\n\n- The cosine of an angle is equal to the adjacent divided by the hypotenuse (C-A-H). Relative to the angle $\\theta,$ the adjacent side is $\\overline{AB},$ and the hypotenuse is $\\overline{BC}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\cos{\\theta} = \\dfrac{AB}{BC} = \\dfrac{4}{5}.\n$$\n\n- The tangent of an angle is equal to the opposite divided by the adjacent (T-O-A). Relative to the angle $\\theta,$ the opposite side is $\\overline{AC},$ and the adjacent side is $\\overline{AB}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\tan{\\theta} = \\dfrac{AC}{AB} = \\dfrac{3}{4}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078538 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ee667b29-0e64-58a9-af5f-3a42e42c422f" "question-28b7c740-c4b9-5ebd-bb70-3180edf82e3a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078253 :question/problem "In the right triangle $\\triangle ABC,$ the angle $\\angle A$ is a right angle, and the side lengths are $AB=2,$ $AC=\\sqrt{5},$ and $BC=3.$ Find $\\tan B.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's illustrate the given triangle.\n\n![](images/4e/4e4e2005e31716a09953aed9054cc5796ee915d41d5a9020042984b348e3b743.png)\n\nThe tangent of an angle is equal to the opposite divided by the adjacent (T-O-A). Relative to $\\angle B,$ the opposite side is $\\overline{AC},$ and the adjacent side is $\\overline{AB}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\tan{B} &= \\dfrac{AC}{AB} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}.\n\t}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078539 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-07f55725-512f-52ff-845b-7dcde64b9b62" "question-3e934f97-b3fe-53b9-be38-8426c7f7fdb2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078251 :question/problem "Given that $\\tan\\theta = \\dfrac{1}{4},$ find the value of $x.$\n\n![](images/f8/f8affbac78c75000d7bbbc8c15508252f7bea0270fdf6cc9c5e5244eb89b505d.png)" :question/worked-solution "The tangent of an angle is equal to the opposite divided by the adjacent (T-O-A).\n\nRelative to the angle $\\theta,$ the length of the opposite side is $x-1,$ and the length of the adjacent side is $2x.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{adjacent}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} & =\\frac{x-1}{2x} \\\\ 2x & =4(x-1) \\\\ 2x & =4x-4 \\\\ 2x & =4 \\\\ x & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078540 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-016edb3d-93e4-5ce6-a38f-b34c506d12dc" "question-8784f120-baa9-5904-bf25-48701c5330e9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078255 :question/problem "Evaluate $\\cos\\left(50^\\circ\\right).$ Round the answer to two decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Using a calculator, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({50}^{∘}) & =0.64278...≈0.64,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-986f7504-f85e-51dd-a6eb-fbd91caed65d" :question/id #uuid "986f7504-f85e-51dd-a6eb-fbd91caed65d" :question/math-academy-id "q-4543" :question/problem "![](images/8d/8d31dc0c38fbd5f1b3a39a53d3d50939421509ddcef45a96e56d2aa367ed4cd8.png)\n\n$\\operatorname{tan}⁡D=$" :question/worked-solution "The tangent of an angle is equal to the opposite divided by the adjacent (T-O-A). Relative to the angle $D,$ the opposite side is $\\overset{―}{BC},$ and the adjacent is $\\overset{―}{BD}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡D & =\\frac{BC}{BD} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-de92e059-1982-5dbc-8af4-37792803768f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-de92e059-1982-5dbc-8af4-37792803768f" :answer-field/id #uuid "de92e059-1982-5dbc-8af4-37792803768f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-89d44df5-6fd3-5f69-a480-93623d68bc39" :answer-field/choices ["answer-503ab61a-d84b-501e-9b52-096bbc2f789a" "answer-ea473308-3ceb-56fe-8dec-e7299e790279" "answer-45fbc98b-11ec-5e5a-9e5f-0eddc342eb73" "answer-89d44df5-6fd3-5f69-a480-93623d68bc39" "answer-24c7aab2-8433-5bef-a4f1-a4b1b2559e22"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-503ab61a-d84b-501e-9b52-096bbc2f789a" :answer/id #uuid "503ab61a-d84b-501e-9b52-096bbc2f789a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea473308-3ceb-56fe-8dec-e7299e790279" :answer/id #uuid "ea473308-3ceb-56fe-8dec-e7299e790279" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45fbc98b-11ec-5e5a-9e5f-0eddc342eb73" :answer/id #uuid "45fbc98b-11ec-5e5a-9e5f-0eddc342eb73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-89d44df5-6fd3-5f69-a480-93623d68bc39" :answer/id #uuid "89d44df5-6fd3-5f69-a480-93623d68bc39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-24c7aab2-8433-5bef-a4f1-a4b1b2559e22" :answer/id #uuid "24c7aab2-8433-5bef-a4f1-a4b1b2559e22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a0ff3000-90f6-50f0-b55e-baca4a2294a7" :question/id #uuid "a0ff3000-90f6-50f0-b55e-baca4a2294a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-4605" :question/problem "![](images/44/44f3144d089201597af3ffe32176741b15cbb2345c635549058148f83781175a.png)\n\n$\\operatorname{cos}⁡E=$" :question/worked-solution "The cosine of an angle is equal to the adjacent divided by the hypotenuse (C-A-H). Relative to the angle $E,$ the adjacent side is $\\overset{―}{FE},$ and the hypotenuse is $\\overset{―}{DE}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡E & =\\frac{FE}{DE}=\\frac{80}{89}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-07898785-a218-597e-baaa-e921663aee93"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-07898785-a218-597e-baaa-e921663aee93" :answer-field/id #uuid "07898785-a218-597e-baaa-e921663aee93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-70dcf41a-bc67-58d9-9b25-43ce1a8d4671" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c6bda1e7-d093-58b4-8e9f-f5cf6a2e2e39" "answer-9a735f61-7395-5cc3-8db3-f9fe94365b06" "answer-70dcf41a-bc67-58d9-9b25-43ce1a8d4671" "answer-6585b2a8-7a2e-566f-ba35-9d2b78d20311" "answer-b6f0ad3b-4204-50b8-9ec6-145cd980bb2f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6bda1e7-d093-58b4-8e9f-f5cf6a2e2e39" :answer/id #uuid "c6bda1e7-d093-58b4-8e9f-f5cf6a2e2e39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{39}{80}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a735f61-7395-5cc3-8db3-f9fe94365b06" :answer/id #uuid "9a735f61-7395-5cc3-8db3-f9fe94365b06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{80}{39}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70dcf41a-bc67-58d9-9b25-43ce1a8d4671" :answer/id #uuid "70dcf41a-bc67-58d9-9b25-43ce1a8d4671" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{80}{89}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6585b2a8-7a2e-566f-ba35-9d2b78d20311" :answer/id #uuid "6585b2a8-7a2e-566f-ba35-9d2b78d20311" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{89}{39}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b6f0ad3b-4204-50b8-9ec6-145cd980bb2f" :answer/id #uuid "b6f0ad3b-4204-50b8-9ec6-145cd980bb2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{89}{80}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ee667b29-0e64-58a9-af5f-3a42e42c422f" :question/id #uuid "ee667b29-0e64-58a9-af5f-3a42e42c422f" :question/math-academy-id "q-54095" :question/problem "![](images/14/14c05d01cdba24b04330a821597eef21dd325228bb8a7fc1e02103ca80f39450.png)\n\n$\\operatorname{cos}⁡S=$" :question/worked-solution "The cosine of an angle is equal to the adjacent divided by the hypotenuse (C-A-H). Relative to the angle $S,$ the adjacent side is $\\overset{―}{ST},$ and the hypotenuse is $\\overset{―}{SR}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡S & =\\frac{ST}{SR} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{19}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{19}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{\\sqrt{19}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{133}}{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1c17fb68-b03e-5969-a875-bcdd0370c517"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1c17fb68-b03e-5969-a875-bcdd0370c517" :answer-field/id #uuid "1c17fb68-b03e-5969-a875-bcdd0370c517" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a5a1d4ab-4862-5d36-85a4-10e29fd32e5b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-31b09780-74f8-5623-9c4b-1d4b88920a31" "answer-807a7948-f38a-5004-a53f-71205609f19e" "answer-70b578e6-30ac-538e-a414-29e486d5b209" "answer-a5a1d4ab-4862-5d36-85a4-10e29fd32e5b" "answer-ff1f13cf-b382-555c-a965-2dabb0abd939"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-31b09780-74f8-5623-9c4b-1d4b88920a31" :answer/id #uuid "31b09780-74f8-5623-9c4b-1d4b88920a31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{14}}{19}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-807a7948-f38a-5004-a53f-71205609f19e" :answer/id #uuid "807a7948-f38a-5004-a53f-71205609f19e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{21}}{19}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70b578e6-30ac-538e-a414-29e486d5b209" :answer/id #uuid "70b578e6-30ac-538e-a414-29e486d5b209" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{112}}{19}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5a1d4ab-4862-5d36-85a4-10e29fd32e5b" :answer/id #uuid "a5a1d4ab-4862-5d36-85a4-10e29fd32e5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{133}}{19}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff1f13cf-b382-555c-a965-2dabb0abd939" :answer/id #uuid "ff1f13cf-b382-555c-a965-2dabb0abd939" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{26}}{19}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-28b7c740-c4b9-5ebd-bb70-3180edf82e3a" :question/id #uuid "28b7c740-c4b9-5ebd-bb70-3180edf82e3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-54107" :question/problem "In the right triangle $△ABC,$ $∠A$ is a right angle, $AB=3\\sqrt{7},$ $AC=9$ and $BC=12.$ Find $\\operatorname{sin}⁡C.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's illustrate the given triangle.\n\n![](images/40/40f31b56b1078bbab7d423c89088218c3fc52e3a2d56c2170c380d415860c2ad.png)\n\nThe sine of an angle is equal to the opposite divided by the hypotenuse (S-O-H). Relative to the angle $C,$ the opposite side is $\\overset{―}{AB},$ and the hypotenuse is $\\overset{―}{CB}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡C & =\\frac{AB}{CB}=\\frac{3\\sqrt{7}}{12}=\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f7c631e7-639a-55f6-b533-553cff151211"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f7c631e7-639a-55f6-b533-553cff151211" :answer-field/id #uuid "f7c631e7-639a-55f6-b533-553cff151211" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0c742ab1-2878-5697-8580-71d0bf6781d9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-459a7d22-49e8-5e65-a53e-608ea8dcbb70" "answer-f950c099-cf0d-5b7d-be55-608c4139a6ee" "answer-00c27cff-6db0-5925-b3a7-892c4c471ebe" "answer-6d0bd988-f8a7-52b7-934e-dd0faff8023c" "answer-0c742ab1-2878-5697-8580-71d0bf6781d9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-459a7d22-49e8-5e65-a53e-608ea8dcbb70" :answer/id #uuid "459a7d22-49e8-5e65-a53e-608ea8dcbb70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f950c099-cf0d-5b7d-be55-608c4139a6ee" :answer/id #uuid "f950c099-cf0d-5b7d-be55-608c4139a6ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-00c27cff-6db0-5925-b3a7-892c4c471ebe" :answer/id #uuid "00c27cff-6db0-5925-b3a7-892c4c471ebe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{21}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d0bd988-f8a7-52b7-934e-dd0faff8023c" :answer/id #uuid "6d0bd988-f8a7-52b7-934e-dd0faff8023c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c742ab1-2878-5697-8580-71d0bf6781d9" :answer/id #uuid "0c742ab1-2878-5697-8580-71d0bf6781d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-07f55725-512f-52ff-845b-7dcde64b9b62" :question/id #uuid "07f55725-512f-52ff-845b-7dcde64b9b62" :question/math-academy-id "q-121893" :question/problem "![](images/e2/e23e1c8331838c31bbf9943d95a313a84ff1a341e9200d78a66c2543fe00cc6d.png)\n\nIf $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{15}{12},$ then $x=$" :question/worked-solution "The tangent of an angle is equal to the opposite divided by the adjacent (T-O-A). \n\nRelative to the angle $\\theta ,$ the length of the opposite side is $6x-5,$ and the length of the adjacent side is $4x.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{adjacent}} \\\\ \\frac{15}{12} & =\\frac{6x-5}{4x} \\\\ 60x & =72x-60 \\\\ 12x & =60 \\\\ x & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dd9dfa97-5736-54f0-a836-6e83defce220"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dd9dfa97-5736-54f0-a836-6e83defce220" :answer-field/id #uuid "dd9dfa97-5736-54f0-a836-6e83defce220" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-685428e6-feeb-5203-b19c-cb5a6c3ab22e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-84a45b8e-205b-58fa-b8a7-69ea3b9a7a7f" "answer-4ede53c3-8e86-5289-a1d5-d65a3304ee50" "answer-11d8f7cd-76de-5c8f-a7e1-4dc87b73db86" "answer-685428e6-feeb-5203-b19c-cb5a6c3ab22e" "answer-162d545d-4902-5d83-958a-e5ca68604c45"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84a45b8e-205b-58fa-b8a7-69ea3b9a7a7f" :answer/id #uuid "84a45b8e-205b-58fa-b8a7-69ea3b9a7a7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ede53c3-8e86-5289-a1d5-d65a3304ee50" :answer/id #uuid "4ede53c3-8e86-5289-a1d5-d65a3304ee50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-11d8f7cd-76de-5c8f-a7e1-4dc87b73db86" :answer/id #uuid "11d8f7cd-76de-5c8f-a7e1-4dc87b73db86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-685428e6-feeb-5203-b19c-cb5a6c3ab22e" :answer/id #uuid "685428e6-feeb-5203-b19c-cb5a6c3ab22e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-162d545d-4902-5d83-958a-e5ca68604c45" :answer/id #uuid "162d545d-4902-5d83-958a-e5ca68604c45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3e934f97-b3fe-53b9-be38-8426c7f7fdb2" :question/id #uuid "3e934f97-b3fe-53b9-be38-8426c7f7fdb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-121889" :question/problem "![](images/d0/d08a4d0946265ba1314831913b7c31de68fb59845fca42b2b79707c04dbd827c.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{5}{8},$ the value of $x$ is" :question/worked-solution "The cosine of an angle is equal to the adjacent divided by the hypotenuse (C-A-H).\n\nRelative to the angle $\\theta ,$ the length of the adjacent side is $\\frac{7}{4}x+29,$ and the length of the hypotenuse is $7x+17.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\text{adjacent}}{\\text{hypotenuse}} \\\\ \\frac{5}{8} & =\\frac{(\\frac{7}{4}x+29)}{7x+17} \\\\ 5(7x+17) & =8(\\frac{7}{4}x+29) \\\\ 35x+85 & =14x+232 \\\\ 21x & =147 \\\\ x & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fdb72b5e-3640-52fa-95f4-ecdf6dcc4bd0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fdb72b5e-3640-52fa-95f4-ecdf6dcc4bd0" :answer-field/id #uuid "fdb72b5e-3640-52fa-95f4-ecdf6dcc4bd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-917c3b75-1fb5-5141-b5d8-7f8a0c0b3eb7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-54889477-a9fd-55c0-bd74-a943ba627d0b" "answer-b9deb636-6da1-5752-81cc-bc8451faac84" "answer-631d6b33-926c-57c5-b3f1-ecb40b7e66be" "answer-917c3b75-1fb5-5141-b5d8-7f8a0c0b3eb7" "answer-eefa9668-3ca9-547b-8410-3ba4c6bf019c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-54889477-a9fd-55c0-bd74-a943ba627d0b" :answer/id #uuid "54889477-a9fd-55c0-bd74-a943ba627d0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b9deb636-6da1-5752-81cc-bc8451faac84" :answer/id #uuid "b9deb636-6da1-5752-81cc-bc8451faac84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-631d6b33-926c-57c5-b3f1-ecb40b7e66be" :answer/id #uuid "631d6b33-926c-57c5-b3f1-ecb40b7e66be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-917c3b75-1fb5-5141-b5d8-7f8a0c0b3eb7" :answer/id #uuid "917c3b75-1fb5-5141-b5d8-7f8a0c0b3eb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eefa9668-3ca9-547b-8410-3ba4c6bf019c" :answer/id #uuid "eefa9668-3ca9-547b-8410-3ba4c6bf019c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-016edb3d-93e4-5ce6-a38f-b34c506d12dc" :question/id #uuid "016edb3d-93e4-5ce6-a38f-b34c506d12dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-264155" :question/problem "Rounded to $3$ decimal places, $\\operatorname{tan}⁡({74}^{∘})≈${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Using a calculator, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡({74}^{∘}) & =3.487\\,414…≈3.487,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9f05efa8-2aa3-5945-b767-a1ff8d5bad66"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9f05efa8-2aa3-5945-b767-a1ff8d5bad66" :answer-field/id #uuid "9f05efa8-2aa3-5945-b767-a1ff8d5bad66" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-94df7301-ea53-57d6-8a9f-955d4e126031" :answer-field/choices ["answer-94df7301-ea53-57d6-8a9f-955d4e126031"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94df7301-ea53-57d6-8a9f-955d4e126031" :answer/id #uuid "94df7301-ea53-57d6-8a9f-955d4e126031" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.487" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8784f120-baa9-5904-bf25-48701c5330e9" :question/id #uuid "8784f120-baa9-5904-bf25-48701c5330e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-264144" :question/problem "Rounded to $3$ decimal places, $\\operatorname{sin}⁡({87}^{∘})≈${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Using a calculator, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({87}^{∘}) & =0.998\\,629…≈0.999,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-accb383e-3441-5045-89e0-bc4d077184d3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-accb383e-3441-5045-89e0-bc4d077184d3" :answer-field/id #uuid "accb383e-3441-5045-89e0-bc4d077184d3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e8786983-46a5-5513-b721-9846e247b148" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e8786983-46a5-5513-b721-9846e247b148"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8786983-46a5-5513-b721-9846e247b148" :answer/id #uuid "e8786983-46a5-5513-b721-9846e247b148" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.999" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186079636 :tutorial/content "Let's remind ourselves of the names of the sides of a right triangle relative to an angle $\\theta.$ \n\n![](images/4c/4cbe48f70bc4bf67600269883c1260cec2181cf01b50a9675c3177b72d7f954b.png)\n\nThe three fundamental trigonometric ratios, **sine**, **cosine**, and **tangent**, represent the ratios of the sides of a right triangle. The ratios are often shortened to $\\sin$, $\\cos,$ and $\\tan,$ and they are defined as\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\sin(\\theta) &= \\dfrac {\\text{opposite}} {\\text{hypotenuse}},  \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\cos(\\theta) &= \\dfrac {\\text{adjacent}} {\\text{hypotenuse}},  \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\tan(\\theta) &= \\dfrac {\\text{opposite}} {\\text{adjacent}}.  \\\n\t}\n$$\n\nFor a given angle $\\theta$, these ratios remain the same no matter what the size of the triangle is. For example, if we were to double the length of each side of a given triangle, the values of these ratios would remain unchanged. \n\nAn easy way of remembering how to compute the different trigonometric ratios is by using the three-syllable acronym **SOH-CAH-TOA**. It stands for:\n\n- SOH $\\rightarrow$ **S**ine = **O**pposite / **H**ypotenuse,\n\n- CAH $\\rightarrow$ **C**osine = **A**djacent / **H**ypotenuse,\n\n- TOA $\\rightarrow$ **T**angent = **O**pposite / **A**djacent." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186079638 :tutorial/content "Calculators usually have a special key that allows us to compute $\\sin\\theta,$ $\\cos\\theta,$ and $\\tan\\theta$ for some specific value of $\\theta.$\n\nFor example, using a calculator, we can compute the trigonometric ratios for $\\theta = 30^\\circ$ and get the following results:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({30}^{∘}) & =0.5 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡({30}^{∘}) & =0.866... \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) & =0.577...\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Watch out!** Make sure that the calculator is in degrees mode (instead of radians mode) before you start the computation." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078639 :activity/expected-seconds 600.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "activity-429544ed-8bbc-5289-a093-2f183882bb3e" :activity/id #uuid "429544ed-8bbc-5289-a093-2f183882bb3e" :activity/title "The Cayley-Hamilton Theorem" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048726 :activity/course 17592186046669 :activity/steps ["step-c9488e67-2747-5299-bfa1-6e5c456d8b59" "step-d76a9bcf-ce1d-59e1-a458-d42736b3c5ac" "step-577e82f8-0c54-5def-a845-15ce9bcbcc0c" "step-009b2545-43e5-5219-8e67-bc5239b87a2f" "step-e5720d7a-1ab9-5e71-a410-d953677a5677"] :activity/first-step "step-c9488e67-2747-5299-bfa1-6e5c456d8b59" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-c9488e67-2747-5299-bfa1-6e5c456d8b59" :step/id #uuid "c9488e67-2747-5299-bfa1-6e5c456d8b59" :step/content 17592186326708 :step/next "step-d76a9bcf-ce1d-59e1-a458-d42736b3c5ac" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d76a9bcf-ce1d-59e1-a458-d42736b3c5ac" :step/id #uuid "d76a9bcf-ce1d-59e1-a458-d42736b3c5ac" :step/content 17592186125140 :step/next "step-577e82f8-0c54-5def-a845-15ce9bcbcc0c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-577e82f8-0c54-5def-a845-15ce9bcbcc0c" :step/id #uuid "577e82f8-0c54-5def-a845-15ce9bcbcc0c" :step/content 17592186392218 :step/next "step-009b2545-43e5-5219-8e67-bc5239b87a2f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-009b2545-43e5-5219-8e67-bc5239b87a2f" :step/id #uuid "009b2545-43e5-5219-8e67-bc5239b87a2f" :step/content 17592186354445 :step/next "step-e5720d7a-1ab9-5e71-a410-d953677a5677" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-e5720d7a-1ab9-5e71-a410-d953677a5677" :step/id #uuid "e5720d7a-1ab9-5e71-a410-d953677a5677" :step/content 17592186354451 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096636 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ef9f41c7-171c-5068-8a8d-ff2c5135b2da" "question-40e64447-ceb6-5045-8392-d608f9b3b14b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ef9f41c7-171c-5068-8a8d-ff2c5135b2da" :question/id #uuid "ef9f41c7-171c-5068-8a8d-ff2c5135b2da" :question/math-academy-id "q-26475" :question/problem "Find the solution to the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2a+3b=-2 \\\\ \\frac{a}{3}-\\frac{b}{6}=-\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the fractions in the second equation, we must multiply the second equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $6.$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2a+3b=-2 \\\\ \\frac{a}{3}-\\frac{b}{6}=-\\frac{5}{3} & |\\,\\times 6\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}2a+3b=-2 \\\\ 2a-b=-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the substitution method to solve the system. Let's solve for $b$ in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a-b & =-10 \\\\ b & =2a+10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can substitute $b=2a+10$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a+3b & =-2 \\\\ 2a+3(2a+10) & =-2 \\\\ 2a+6a+30 & =-2 \\\\ 8a & =-32 \\\\ a & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $b,$ we substitute $a=-4$ into the equation $b=2a+10$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =2a+10 \\\\  & =2(-4)+10 \\\\  & =-8+10 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=-4,\\,b=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4e76924e-7974-5bfd-a8ee-f608b55003f8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4e76924e-7974-5bfd-a8ee-f608b55003f8" :answer-field/id #uuid "4e76924e-7974-5bfd-a8ee-f608b55003f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2f67813b-4012-57a6-aa60-6e1f4b03c49b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4931d63f-6063-5b84-9f38-d5b26851222a" "answer-8ac277a4-9539-5e8e-a05e-de4f499992b3" "answer-2f67813b-4012-57a6-aa60-6e1f4b03c49b" "answer-b09fc133-c399-5f21-8549-810bcfd05f1a" "answer-e66e2e44-a83a-5b53-8541-fd9e66215cf5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4931d63f-6063-5b84-9f38-d5b26851222a" :answer/id #uuid "4931d63f-6063-5b84-9f38-d5b26851222a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=-2,\\,b=6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ac277a4-9539-5e8e-a05e-de4f499992b3" :answer/id #uuid "8ac277a4-9539-5e8e-a05e-de4f499992b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=-3,\\,b=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f67813b-4012-57a6-aa60-6e1f4b03c49b" :answer/id #uuid "2f67813b-4012-57a6-aa60-6e1f4b03c49b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=-4,\\,b=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b09fc133-c399-5f21-8549-810bcfd05f1a" :answer/id #uuid "b09fc133-c399-5f21-8549-810bcfd05f1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=0,\\,b=-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e66e2e44-a83a-5b53-8541-fd9e66215cf5" :answer/id #uuid "e66e2e44-a83a-5b53-8541-fd9e66215cf5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=2,\\,b=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096635 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-be4c74c9-6e39-5f39-a1ce-fbc98923b17f" "question-b1b90563-ce29-5141-8ac6-0ac20bb77c12"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-be4c74c9-6e39-5f39-a1ce-fbc98923b17f" :question/id #uuid "be4c74c9-6e39-5f39-a1ce-fbc98923b17f" :question/math-academy-id "q-52203" :question/problem "Find the solution to the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-\\frac{2}{7}y=2 \\\\ -x+\\frac{2}{9}y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of fractions, we multiply the first equation by $7$ and the second equation by $9,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-\\frac{2}{7}y=2 & |\\times 7 \\\\ -x+\\frac{2}{9}y=2 & |\\times 9\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}7x-2y=14 \\\\ -9x+2y=18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. We can eliminate $y$ by adding the two equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x-\\cancel{2y} & =14 \\\\ -9x+\\cancel{2y} & =18 \\\\ (7x-9x) & =(14+18) \\\\ -2x & =32 \\\\ x & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $x=-16$ into the first equation to solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x-2y & =14 \\\\ 7(-16)-2y & =14 \\\\ -112-2y & =14 \\\\ -2y & =126 \\\\ y & =-63\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system is $x=-16$ and $y=-63.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-61aac299-670f-5a9c-bbec-1956ec185e42"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-61aac299-670f-5a9c-bbec-1956ec185e42" :answer-field/id #uuid "61aac299-670f-5a9c-bbec-1956ec185e42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0699480b-fcdd-5aa7-bd88-db69b130f0d4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6bef9576-7456-5c97-8c11-0c2e8958fa4f" "answer-0699480b-fcdd-5aa7-bd88-db69b130f0d4" "answer-b57c8f87-09f5-526e-925b-2fa685384d43" "answer-cbca4dac-d673-5f55-816e-2823843ec578" "answer-8db89ec1-822e-58c5-b2f7-ab0ed448f0e4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6bef9576-7456-5c97-8c11-0c2e8958fa4f" :answer/id #uuid "6bef9576-7456-5c97-8c11-0c2e8958fa4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-12,\\,y=-48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0699480b-fcdd-5aa7-bd88-db69b130f0d4" :answer/id #uuid "0699480b-fcdd-5aa7-bd88-db69b130f0d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-16,\\,y=-63" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b57c8f87-09f5-526e-925b-2fa685384d43" :answer/id #uuid "b57c8f87-09f5-526e-925b-2fa685384d43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-32,\\,y=-26" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cbca4dac-d673-5f55-816e-2823843ec578" :answer/id #uuid "cbca4dac-d673-5f55-816e-2823843ec578" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-63,\\,y=-16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8db89ec1-822e-58c5-b2f7-ab0ed448f0e4" :answer/id #uuid "8db89ec1-822e-58c5-b2f7-ab0ed448f0e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=16,\\,y=32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096637 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c2c2c978-aae7-58d4-874a-c874d05efc9b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c2c2c978-aae7-58d4-874a-c874d05efc9b" :question/id #uuid "c2c2c978-aae7-58d4-874a-c874d05efc9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-75861" :question/problem "Find the solution to the  following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{4}y=-1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}x+\\frac{1}{2}y=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of fractions, we multiply the first equation by $4$ and the second equation by $6,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{4}y=-1 & |\\times 4 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}x+\\frac{1}{2}y=-6 & |\\times 6\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y=-4 \\\\ 2x+3y=-36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $-1,$ then we will get a $-2x$ term that can cancel with the $2x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y=-4 & |\\,\\times (-1) \\\\ 2x+3y=-36 & \\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+y=4 \\\\ 2x+3y=-36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $x$-variable, and allows us to solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{-2x}+y & =4 \\\\ \\cancel{2x}+3y & =-36 \\\\ (y+3y) & =(4-36) \\\\ 4y & =-32 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{32}{4} \\\\ y & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y=-8$ into the first equation to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-y & =-4 \\\\ 2x-(-8) & =-4 \\\\ 2x+8 & =-4 \\\\ 2x & =-12 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{12}{2} \\\\ x & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system is $x=-6,\\,y=-8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e1e0f312-cd0e-5c8b-a953-be01ee2625b0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e1e0f312-cd0e-5c8b-a953-be01ee2625b0" :answer-field/id #uuid "e1e0f312-cd0e-5c8b-a953-be01ee2625b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b92976d9-53dd-5053-b478-c050ea85c203" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6e086611-7bec-50f9-b80f-9f7d167a7576" "answer-b92976d9-53dd-5053-b478-c050ea85c203" "answer-cd47a55d-6fb7-5018-956e-7585cfc1af31" "answer-b01ccc0c-d6e0-5c8b-8e5f-f9b6e7de0c3b" "answer-8ca432f5-bc7b-5a9d-8960-0c52d5ad9bb8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e086611-7bec-50f9-b80f-9f7d167a7576" :answer/id #uuid "6e086611-7bec-50f9-b80f-9f7d167a7576" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-3,\\,y=-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b92976d9-53dd-5053-b478-c050ea85c203" :answer/id #uuid "b92976d9-53dd-5053-b478-c050ea85c203" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-6,\\,y=-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd47a55d-6fb7-5018-956e-7585cfc1af31" :answer/id #uuid "cd47a55d-6fb7-5018-956e-7585cfc1af31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=3,\\,y=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b01ccc0c-d6e0-5c8b-8e5f-f9b6e7de0c3b" :answer/id #uuid "b01ccc0c-d6e0-5c8b-8e5f-f9b6e7de0c3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=4,\\,y=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ca432f5-bc7b-5a9d-8960-0c52d5ad9bb8" :answer/id #uuid "8ca432f5-bc7b-5a9d-8960-0c52d5ad9bb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=8,\\,y=-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-40e64447-ceb6-5045-8392-d608f9b3b14b" :question/id #uuid "40e64447-ceb6-5045-8392-d608f9b3b14b" :question/math-academy-id "q-208827" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-5y=7 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{3}+4y=-\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the system of equations given above.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the fractions in the second equation, we must multiply the second equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $3.$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-5y=7 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{3}+4y=-\\frac{8}{3} & |\\,\\times 3\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}x-5y=7 \\\\ 2x+12y=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the substitution method to solve the system. Let's solve for $x$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-5y & =7 \\\\ x & =5y+7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can substitute $x=5y+7$ into the second equation and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+12y & =-8 \\\\ 2(5y+7)+12y & =-8 \\\\ 10y+14+12y & =-8 \\\\ 22y+14 & =-8 \\\\ 22y & =-22 \\\\ y & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $x,$ we substitute $y=-1$ into the equation $x=5y+7,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =5y+7 \\\\  & =5(-1)+7 \\\\  & =-5+7 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=2,\\,y=-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-80927105-5be2-594a-95d0-2c7fe3bfa8ca" "answer-field-76226d76-f5d2-55d4-8a7f-5814323e67f0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-80927105-5be2-594a-95d0-2c7fe3bfa8ca" :answer-field/id #uuid "80927105-5be2-594a-95d0-2c7fe3bfa8ca" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-4a7bd31c-5ecb-5b23-90cc-98381162c779" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4a7bd31c-5ecb-5b23-90cc-98381162c779"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a7bd31c-5ecb-5b23-90cc-98381162c779" :answer/id #uuid "4a7bd31c-5ecb-5b23-90cc-98381162c779" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-76226d76-f5d2-55d4-8a7f-5814323e67f0" :answer-field/id #uuid "76226d76-f5d2-55d4-8a7f-5814323e67f0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-98f282bc-fb6e-570b-ac24-148369f2484f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-98f282bc-fb6e-570b-ac24-148369f2484f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-98f282bc-fb6e-570b-ac24-148369f2484f" :answer/id #uuid "98f282bc-fb6e-570b-ac24-148369f2484f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b1b90563-ce29-5141-8ac6-0ac20bb77c12" :question/id #uuid "b1b90563-ce29-5141-8ac6-0ac20bb77c12" :question/math-academy-id "q-216312" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{4}p+3q=25 \\\\ p+\\frac{2}{5}q=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,q=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of fractions, we multiply the first equation by $4$ and the second equation by $5,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{4}p+3q=25 & |\\times 4 \\\\ p+\\frac{2}{5}q=0 & |\\times 5\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}5p+12q=100 \\\\ 5p+2q=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $-1,$ then we will get a $-5p$ term that can cancel with the $5p$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5p+12q=100 & |\\,\\times (-1) \\\\ 5p+2q=0 & \\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}-5p-12q=-100 \\\\ 5p+2q=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $p$-variable, and allows us to solve for $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{-5p}-12q & =-100 \\\\ \\cancel{5p}+2q & =0 \\\\ (-12q+2q) & =(-100+0) \\\\ -10q & =-100 \\\\ q & =\\frac{100}{10} \\\\ q & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $q=10$ into the second equation to solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5p+2q & =0 \\\\ 5p+2\\cdot 10 & =0 \\\\ 5p+20 & =0 \\\\ 5p & =-20 \\\\ p & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system is $p=-4,\\,q=10.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-28c5e5b8-30fa-5781-8559-a9e4f5d972ae" "answer-field-08b0a80b-6e11-58dd-a2f8-eea08773e1f7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-28c5e5b8-30fa-5781-8559-a9e4f5d972ae" :answer-field/id #uuid "28c5e5b8-30fa-5781-8559-a9e4f5d972ae" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-954a215e-6bc2-56e2-86bb-f73d149f278b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-954a215e-6bc2-56e2-86bb-f73d149f278b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-954a215e-6bc2-56e2-86bb-f73d149f278b" :answer/id #uuid "954a215e-6bc2-56e2-86bb-f73d149f278b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-08b0a80b-6e11-58dd-a2f8-eea08773e1f7" :answer-field/id #uuid "08b0a80b-6e11-58dd-a2f8