ligned}4[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-16 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]\\ne [\\begin{aligned}-16 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there is no $t$ such that \n $2{a}_{1}+t{a}_{2}=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a8913bcd-9ea3-5176-be5c-767230b5bdc3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a8913bcd-9ea3-5176-be5c-767230b5bdc3" :answer-field/id #uuid "a8913bcd-9ea3-5176-be5c-767230b5bdc3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7b39a89b-9b8d-52a3-9357-588262651bee" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e217e4b1-a0b0-5f52-9881-b8ba9a5204d2" "answer-c3245f41-6987-5e17-b6c5-0c173f25056e" "answer-91df5346-a42d-5fd9-a5ba-0704fb0cc455" "answer-027b8325-bddf-5f10-927c-27e8a8d93f7f" "answer-7b39a89b-9b8d-52a3-9357-588262651bee"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e217e4b1-a0b0-5f52-9881-b8ba9a5204d2" :answer/id #uuid "e217e4b1-a0b0-5f52-9881-b8ba9a5204d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3245f41-6987-5e17-b6c5-0c173f25056e" :answer/id #uuid "c3245f41-6987-5e17-b6c5-0c173f25056e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-91df5346-a42d-5fd9-a5ba-0704fb0cc455" :answer/id #uuid "91df5346-a42d-5fd9-a5ba-0704fb0cc455" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-027b8325-bddf-5f10-927c-27e8a8d93f7f" :answer/id #uuid "027b8325-bddf-5f10-927c-27e8a8d93f7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7b39a89b-9b8d-52a3-9357-588262651bee" :answer/id #uuid "7b39a89b-9b8d-52a3-9357-588262651bee" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119806 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7b8162a3-2a18-5498-a3a6-ab4fdf90d980"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7b8162a3-2a18-5498-a3a6-ab4fdf90d980" :question/id #uuid "7b8162a3-2a18-5498-a3a6-ab4fdf90d980" :question/math-academy-id "q-105158" :question/problem "Find $x$, if $5a-2x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5a-2x & =b \\\\ -2x & =b-5a \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}(b-5a) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]-5[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-167770ed-e7de-54b6-9bfa-73c5e3df3786"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-167770ed-e7de-54b6-9bfa-73c5e3df3786" :answer-field/id #uuid "167770ed-e7de-54b6-9bfa-73c5e3df3786" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-77982fef-cbd9-5b64-9beb-aef93c81e8b7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e9436cfd-df38-58b3-bdb8-5acac9079d34" "answer-02aca304-7b48-53d3-b89a-9ec1254a925a" "answer-bb24ab63-f2c2-5312-9f4a-1f89c660eb2b" "answer-c9cf2b8d-50b4-5dea-8cdb-f6d96e285ac9" "answer-77982fef-cbd9-5b64-9beb-aef93c81e8b7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9436cfd-df38-58b3-bdb8-5acac9079d34" :answer/id #uuid "e9436cfd-df38-58b3-bdb8-5acac9079d34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02aca304-7b48-53d3-b89a-9ec1254a925a" :answer/id #uuid "02aca304-7b48-53d3-b89a-9ec1254a925a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bb24ab63-f2c2-5312-9f4a-1f89c660eb2b" :answer/id #uuid "bb24ab63-f2c2-5312-9f4a-1f89c660eb2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9cf2b8d-50b4-5dea-8cdb-f6d96e285ac9" :answer/id #uuid "c9cf2b8d-50b4-5dea-8cdb-f6d96e285ac9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77982fef-cbd9-5b64-9beb-aef93c81e8b7" :answer/id #uuid "77982fef-cbd9-5b64-9beb-aef93c81e8b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119807 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f9fda870-d2c0-5b67-a720-dd733f4059b5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f9fda870-d2c0-5b67-a720-dd733f4059b5" :question/id #uuid "f9fda870-d2c0-5b67-a720-dd733f4059b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-105163" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1} \\\\ 7{x}_{1} \\\\ -{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ 7{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ 7{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $(-2)$ and adding the result to the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1} & =-9\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}_{1}=3$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(3)+2{x}_{2} & =4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-\\frac{11}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{11}{2}$ into the third equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} & =-11 \\\\ -(3)+3(-\\frac{11}{2}) & =-11 \\\\ -\\frac{33}{2} & =-8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a false statement. \n\nSo, the system has no solution." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-036cd528-ad80-51a8-8b57-1c098a2a1799"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-036cd528-ad80-51a8-8b57-1c098a2a1799" :answer-field/id #uuid "036cd528-ad80-51a8-8b57-1c098a2a1799" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a534e8f3-d655-5502-bc89-53c81026a425" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9dfb10a9-8436-5e35-b531-240827bbf3d9" "answer-d28d263f-fd3b-5140-9893-862b22fa936d" "answer-bd9c2754-dc15-56f5-8e26-d514db78cd49" "answer-eb547a3b-90e6-5909-88af-1af5468ae682" "answer-a534e8f3-d655-5502-bc89-53c81026a425"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9dfb10a9-8436-5e35-b531-240827bbf3d9" :answer/id #uuid "9dfb10a9-8436-5e35-b531-240827bbf3d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d28d263f-fd3b-5140-9893-862b22fa936d" :answer/id #uuid "d28d263f-fd3b-5140-9893-862b22fa936d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd9c2754-dc15-56f5-8e26-d514db78cd49" :answer/id #uuid "bd9c2754-dc15-56f5-8e26-d514db78cd49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb547a3b-90e6-5909-88af-1af5468ae682" :answer/id #uuid "eb547a3b-90e6-5909-88af-1af5468ae682" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a534e8f3-d655-5502-bc89-53c81026a425" :answer/id #uuid "a534e8f3-d655-5502-bc89-53c81026a425" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120309 :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}=3 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 5 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 5 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}=3 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-3$ and from the second equation we get ${x}_{2}=3.$ Substituting these into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3+2(-3)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=11.\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=11$, ${x}_{2}=3$, and ${x}_{3}=-3,$ which means \n\n$$\n11{a}_{1}+3{a}_{2}-3{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=11+3-3=11.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186117993 :answer-field/correct 17592186117998 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068843 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c9000a57-600a-5a19-a505-3e46af6f2315"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c9000a57-600a-5a19-a505-3e46af6f2315" :question/id #uuid "c9000a57-600a-5a19-a505-3e46af6f2315" :question/math-academy-id "q-158615" :question/problem "![](images/a3/a3e86e25d02f4bf51f0f1fcad5f3be92dc87141b0ae1bf775eb3b9ec9d05aa28.png)\n\nGiven that $r$, $s$ and $t$ in the above diagram are parallel, find $m∠1.$" :question/worked-solution "Consider $∠2$ and $∠3$ in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/44/44552b4c1624cd049769bf672d510c33f5cfdb53a8726ada5e0ed4cafea11b64.png)\n\nNote that $∠2$ and the angle whose measure is ${80}^{∘}$ are corresponding angles formed by the same transversal. Therefore, \n\n$$\nm∠2={80}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, note that $∠3$ and the angle whose measure is ${50}^{∘}$ are corresponding angles formed by the same transversal. Therefore, \n\n$$\nm∠3={50}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nLet's add these measures to our diagram:\n\n![](images/46/4672d1aa0d64c5af11c85bb90f834a440eb53a4b9e490ce1b0cb22b5306f4f27.png)\n\nThe angles $∠1$, $∠2,$ and $∠3$ combined give a straight angle. So, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠1+m∠2+m∠3 & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠1+{80}^{∘}+{50}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠1+{130}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠1 & ={50}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-96e90e80-750f-5c33-af90-c6f2fdc5beb0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-96e90e80-750f-5c33-af90-c6f2fdc5beb0" :answer-field/id #uuid "96e90e80-750f-5c33-af90-c6f2fdc5beb0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-30be860f-294c-572c-bce5-95a3b5737ac7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-86e315ee-aeba-5949-923f-bf63d52c529b" "answer-866eb1ee-dc57-51fd-ad60-d807bbc84f2c" "answer-30be860f-294c-572c-bce5-95a3b5737ac7" "answer-5ca2efe0-3545-5059-bdae-7dba0a5c0d86" "answer-ae95af60-a0a8-52e4-92f0-f0dd33e08da9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-86e315ee-aeba-5949-923f-bf63d52c529b" :answer/id #uuid "86e315ee-aeba-5949-923f-bf63d52c529b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{40}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-866eb1ee-dc57-51fd-ad60-d807bbc84f2c" :answer/id #uuid "866eb1ee-dc57-51fd-ad60-d807bbc84f2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-30be860f-294c-572c-bce5-95a3b5737ac7" :answer/id #uuid "30be860f-294c-572c-bce5-95a3b5737ac7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{50}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ca2efe0-3545-5059-bdae-7dba0a5c0d86" :answer/id #uuid "5ca2efe0-3545-5059-bdae-7dba0a5c0d86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae95af60-a0a8-52e4-92f0-f0dd33e08da9" :answer/id #uuid "ae95af60-a0a8-52e4-92f0-f0dd33e08da9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{65}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147475 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ae3f3bc6-d6de-5132-b72c-58e7d4ad1247"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ae3f3bc6-d6de-5132-b72c-58e7d4ad1247" :question/id #uuid "ae3f3bc6-d6de-5132-b72c-58e7d4ad1247" :question/math-academy-id "q-318218" :question/problem "A startup launched its website with $25$ initial visitors. An exponential model estimates that at the end of each day after launch, the number of visitors increased by $300%$ of the number of visitors at the end of the previous day.\n\nAccording to this model, how many visitors are there estimated to be after $3$ days?" :question/worked-solution "The number of visitors $V(t)$ grows exponentially with a growth rate of $300%.$\n\nLet's write down what we know:\n\n- $a=25$ is the total number of visitors initially\n\n- $r=3.0$ is the growth rate ($300%$ expressed as a decimal)\n\n- $t=$ the time (in days) after launch\n\nThe formula for exponential growth is\n\n$$\nV=a(1+r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $V(t)$ is\n\n$$\nV=25\\cdot (1+3.0)^{t}.\n$$\n\nSimplifying the above, we get\n\n$$\nV(t)=25\\cdot (4)^{t}.\n$$\n\nTo find the total number of visitors after $3$ days, we evaluate the above for $t=3:$\n\n$$\nV(3)=25\\cdot (4)^{3}=25\\cdot 64=1600\n$$\n\nTherefore, the estimated number of visitors after $3$ days is $1600.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bb13cd8f-4bfe-5cf0-87bd-31c8b6751181"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bb13cd8f-4bfe-5cf0-87bd-31c8b6751181" :answer-field/id #uuid "bb13cd8f-4bfe-5cf0-87bd-31c8b6751181" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-64224246-717b-5560-a439-97bc68a4601a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b9a93281-cda3-5b66-b8b0-a54453147b96" "answer-d89aba5c-507d-5e93-88e0-2c36f6628884" "answer-64224246-717b-5560-a439-97bc68a4601a" "answer-986c11de-e9ae-55a9-9b24-c86955a2e00c" "answer-5d70b0c2-9ee0-5713-bdcd-7f915663c94f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b9a93281-cda3-5b66-b8b0-a54453147b96" :answer/id #uuid "b9a93281-cda3-5b66-b8b0-a54453147b96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "100" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d89aba5c-507d-5e93-88e0-2c36f6628884" :answer/id #uuid "d89aba5c-507d-5e93-88e0-2c36f6628884" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1200" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64224246-717b-5560-a439-97bc68a4601a" :answer/id #uuid "64224246-717b-5560-a439-97bc68a4601a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1600" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-986c11de-e9ae-55a9-9b24-c86955a2e00c" :answer/id #uuid "986c11de-e9ae-55a9-9b24-c86955a2e00c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2000" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d70b0c2-9ee0-5713-bdcd-7f915663c94f" :answer/id #uuid "5d70b0c2-9ee0-5713-bdcd-7f915663c94f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "800" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152143 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-306ea2e9-4291-50e8-bb35-b93734ac5dfd"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-306ea2e9-4291-50e8-bb35-b93734ac5dfd" :question/id #uuid "306ea2e9-4291-50e8-bb35-b93734ac5dfd" :question/math-academy-id "q-68235" :question/problem "The relationship between the number of cars $n$ Steve washes in $t$ hours is shown in the following table:\n\n| Hours  ($t$) | Cars ($n$) |\n| --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $4$ |\n| $3$ | $12$ |\n| $5$ | $20$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. There is **not** a proportional relationship between $n$ and $t.$\n\nII. The constant of proportionality is $4.$\n\nIII. There is a proportional relationship between $n$ and $t.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's add a new column to our table and compute the ratio of cars per hour for each row.     \n\n| Hours ($t$) | Cars ($n$) | Cars / Hours |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $4$ | $4$ |\n| $3$ | $12$ | $4$ |\n| $5$ | $20$ | $4$ |\n\nThe ratio of cars per hour is the same for each row. Therefore, there is a proportional relationship between $n$ and $t.$ The constant of proportionality is $4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III  only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-86286b5a-e33b-5ac6-883c-ca49e5076c05"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-86286b5a-e33b-5ac6-883c-ca49e5076c05" :answer-field/id #uuid "86286b5a-e33b-5ac6-883c-ca49e5076c05" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-91d5eceb-d8bf-5c1a-bcda-cb3fda2260b2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-eb50758d-969d-5759-9718-9e73629b0cfb" "answer-2548f51d-4886-5ab4-a0aa-259dede06d1d" "answer-91d5eceb-d8bf-5c1a-bcda-cb3fda2260b2" "answer-b1ef4122-304e-5551-a860-fe850fcd736f" "answer-89bbe806-9f01-5394-9ae7-393e3a9c533f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb50758d-969d-5759-9718-9e73629b0cfb" :answer/id #uuid "eb50758d-969d-5759-9718-9e73629b0cfb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2548f51d-4886-5ab4-a0aa-259dede06d1d" :answer/id #uuid "2548f51d-4886-5ab4-a0aa-259dede06d1d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-91d5eceb-d8bf-5c1a-bcda-cb3fda2260b2" :answer/id #uuid "91d5eceb-d8bf-5c1a-bcda-cb3fda2260b2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1ef4122-304e-5551-a860-fe850fcd736f" :answer/id #uuid "b1ef4122-304e-5551-a860-fe850fcd736f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-89bbe806-9f01-5394-9ae7-393e3a9c533f" :answer/id #uuid "89bbe806-9f01-5394-9ae7-393e3a9c533f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110792 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2eafcea3-29cb-5583-a92c-83cb3e6d71ca"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2eafcea3-29cb-5583-a92c-83cb3e6d71ca" :question/id #uuid "2eafcea3-29cb-5583-a92c-83cb3e6d71ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-120503" :question/problem "![](images/fa/fa455c343dc5e6fea5fe9fee9b22b0cfa0ef098c1fb7ae8ea361d9db78e5cc1b.png)\n\nWhat is a correct congruence statement for the pentagons shown in the diagram above?" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $∠A≅∠B≅∠C.$ \n\nLet's determine the vertices in the second pentagon that correspond to $A.$ First, notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =QR \\\\ EA & =RS \\\\ ∠A & ≅∠R\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- vertex $A$ corresponds to vertex $R.$\n\nSimilarly, for vertices in the second pentagon that correspond to $C.$ First, notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =PQ \\\\ CD & =PT \\\\ ∠C & ≅∠P\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- vertex $C$ corresponds to vertex $P,$\n\n- consequently, vertex $B$ corresponds to vertex $Q.$\n\nAs for the other two vertices, notice we have two more pairs of congruent angles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∠D & ≅∠T \\\\ ∠E & ≅∠S.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we have one more pair of congruent sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DE & =TS.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n- vertex $D$ corresponds to vertex $T,$\n\n- vertex $E$ corresponds to vertex $S.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that a correct congruence statement is\n\n$$\nABCDE≅RQPTS.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6c6617e7-0732-53e7-959c-dee6b48142a7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6c6617e7-0732-53e7-959c-dee6b48142a7" :answer-field/id #uuid "6c6617e7-0732-53e7-959c-dee6b48142a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5b6a654e-2365-5f7f-a435-a846a7fadc75" :answer-field/choices ["answer-42593292-dd65-5c9d-90ae-9bcc91722342" "answer-1d45b5bf-815f-54cb-95a6-d1dc8df96e50" "answer-a8c786f0-f9c4-5209-85c4-392d3966bdbb" "answer-281c5c39-1c83-5ee5-9f4d-3d1e3b994d69" "answer-5b6a654e-2365-5f7f-a435-a846a7fadc75"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-42593292-dd65-5c9d-90ae-9bcc91722342" :answer/id #uuid "42593292-dd65-5c9d-90ae-9bcc91722342" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "ABCDE≅PQRST" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d45b5bf-815f-54cb-95a6-d1dc8df96e50" :answer/id #uuid "1d45b5bf-815f-54cb-95a6-d1dc8df96e50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "ABCDE≅PTSRQ" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8c786f0-f9c4-5209-85c4-392d3966bdbb" :answer/id #uuid "a8c786f0-f9c4-5209-85c4-392d3966bdbb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "ABCDE≅QPTSR" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-281c5c39-1c83-5ee5-9f4d-3d1e3b994d69" :answer/id #uuid "281c5c39-1c83-5ee5-9f4d-3d1e3b994d69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "ABCDE≅QRSTP" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b6a654e-2365-5f7f-a435-a846a7fadc75" :answer/id #uuid "5b6a654e-2365-5f7f-a435-a846a7fadc75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "ABCDE≅RQPTS" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059638 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9c716292-5467-511e-9d08-e7988cf3fd66"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9c716292-5467-511e-9d08-e7988cf3fd66" :question/id #uuid "9c716292-5467-511e-9d08-e7988cf3fd66" :question/math-academy-id "q-119313" :question/problem "![](images/10/1073020fe8576784ed24601864f8546a72b426d8f02670b1a8c13923dc16e35f.png)\n\nThe perimeter of the triangle above is $30+15\\sqrt{2}.$ Find the measure of the hypotenuse." :question/worked-solution "Because the triangle is isosceles, the legs must have the same length. Let $a$ be the length of each leg. So, we have\n\n$$\nAB=BC=a.\n$$\n\nMoreover, because the triangle is a *right* isosceles triangle, the hypotenuse must be equal to $\\sqrt{2}$ times the length of a leg. Therefore,\n\n$$\nAC=AB\\cdot \\sqrt{2}=a\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since the perimeter is $p=30+15\\sqrt{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =AB+BC+AC \\\\ 30+15\\sqrt{2} & =a+a+a\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 30+15\\sqrt{2} & =2a+a\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 15(2+\\sqrt{2}) & =a(2+\\sqrt{2}) \\\\ 15\\cancel{(2+\\sqrt{2})} & =a\\cancel{(2+\\sqrt{2})} \\\\ 15 & =a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of each leg is $a=15,$ and the length of the hypotenuse is\n\n$$\nAC=a\\sqrt{2}=15\\sqrt{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-91ed0fd0-f788-5c51-8051-a72f994211f6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-91ed0fd0-f788-5c51-8051-a72f994211f6" :answer-field/id #uuid "91ed0fd0-f788-5c51-8051-a72f994211f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-06c0ec9e-7d1d-56eb-9201-b278b8083e12" :answer-field/choices ["answer-206766d4-4825-5519-b18f-f317696dbba0" "answer-06c0ec9e-7d1d-56eb-9201-b278b8083e12" "answer-c78d1b86-ab77-5b21-a756-f45a9899b3da" "answer-7cc58171-581b-5ece-b94c-184f252d6ece" "answer-0dd6386c-10da-55b4-9934-5b78e4b6448a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-206766d4-4825-5519-b18f-f317696dbba0" :answer/id #uuid "206766d4-4825-5519-b18f-f317696dbba0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06c0ec9e-7d1d-56eb-9201-b278b8083e12" :answer/id #uuid "06c0ec9e-7d1d-56eb-9201-b278b8083e12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure