-dcec978f-3c53-5fe2-812a-19053c19675f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-98cd6248-dbbd-5c94-8f56-d826f45e58ba" "answer-47757023-cf17-574c-a434-8c9fe4c08b36" "answer-dcec978f-3c53-5fe2-812a-19053c19675f" "answer-4656ae6e-ba54-58ef-9045-3c8b22ec6431" "answer-41027a8b-52ba-5683-92a3-eafe05f3ae05"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-98cd6248-dbbd-5c94-8f56-d826f45e58ba" :answer/id #uuid "98cd6248-dbbd-5c94-8f56-d826f45e58ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47757023-cf17-574c-a434-8c9fe4c08b36" :answer/id #uuid "47757023-cf17-574c-a434-8c9fe4c08b36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{49}{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dcec978f-3c53-5fe2-812a-19053c19675f" :answer/id #uuid "dcec978f-3c53-5fe2-812a-19053c19675f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4656ae6e-ba54-58ef-9045-3c8b22ec6431" :answer/id #uuid "4656ae6e-ba54-58ef-9045-3c8b22ec6431" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{{s}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41027a8b-52ba-5683-92a3-eafe05f3ae05" :answer/id #uuid "41027a8b-52ba-5683-92a3-eafe05f3ae05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{s}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147576 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0548a4d1-2f13-56af-b405-5e95b48898dc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-0548a4d1-2f13-56af-b405-5e95b48898dc" :question/id #uuid "0548a4d1-2f13-56af-b405-5e95b48898dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-185132" :question/problem "What is the missing number?\n\n{{field-1}}\n$\\times \\,45%=18$" :question/worked-solution "The part is $18,$ the percentage is $45%,$ and we need to find the whole.\n\nTo do this, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{whole}=\\text{part}÷\\text{percentage}\n$$\n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $45%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{45}{100}=\\frac{45÷5}{100÷5}=\\frac{9}{20}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =18÷45% \\\\  & =18÷\\frac{9}{20} \\\\  & =18\\times \\frac{20}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{9}\\times 20 \\\\  & =2\\times 20 \\\\  & =40\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $40.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-45030650-b785-5cf2-af99-5118e8983acf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-45030650-b785-5cf2-af99-5118e8983acf" :answer-field/id #uuid "45030650-b785-5cf2-af99-5118e8983acf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-26a74301-a239-58fe-bac4-59ef077f5caf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-26a74301-a239-58fe-bac4-59ef077f5caf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26a74301-a239-58fe-bac4-59ef077f5caf" :answer/id #uuid "26a74301-a239-58fe-bac4-59ef077f5caf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "40" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073752 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0c604a3f-ba93-531d-b858-55cd303f28fb"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-0c604a3f-ba93-531d-b858-55cd303f28fb" :question/id #uuid "0c604a3f-ba93-531d-b858-55cd303f28fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-171693" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-u+v=-1 \\\\ 3u+3v=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(u,v)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(u,v)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. It doesn't matter which equation we pick first, so we choose the easiest one. In this case, the first equation looks like the easiest.\n\nUsing the first equation, we can isolate $v$ by adding $u$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\nv=u-1\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $v$ with $u-1$ in the second equation and solve for $u:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3u+3v & =5 \\\\ 3u+3(u-1) & =5 \\\\ 3u+3u-3 & =5 \\\\ 6u & =8 \\\\ u & =\\frac{8}{6} \\\\ u & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $u=\\frac{4}{3}$ into $v=u-1,$ then we can find the value of $v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u-1 \\\\ v & =\\frac{4}{3}-1 \\\\ v & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $u=\\frac{4}{3},\\,v=\\frac{1}{3},$ which can be expressed as $(\\frac{4}{3},\\frac{1}{3}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6fa9b71f-16a8-5365-939e-286334c0da13" "answer-field-1ec83012-bcf1-5281-8dc2-cacc9a39a8f8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6fa9b71f-16a8-5365-939e-286334c0da13" :answer-field/id #uuid "6fa9b71f-16a8-5365-939e-286334c0da13" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-4e269c2f-73d0-5d44-9589-0f161207e171" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4e269c2f-73d0-5d44-9589-0f161207e171"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e269c2f-73d0-5d44-9589-0f161207e171" :answer/id #uuid "4e269c2f-73d0-5d44-9589-0f161207e171" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1ec83012-bcf1-5281-8dc2-cacc9a39a8f8" :answer-field/id #uuid "1ec83012-bcf1-5281-8dc2-cacc9a39a8f8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ec95d12b-ebdc-5ac8-946c-8865c36899a6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ec95d12b-ebdc-5ac8-946c-8865c36899a6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec95d12b-ebdc-5ac8-946c-8865c36899a6" :answer/id #uuid "ec95d12b-ebdc-5ac8-946c-8865c36899a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068682 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-894f2b41-1597-5b67-ba7a-303a5bd60b9b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-894f2b41-1597-5b67-ba7a-303a5bd60b9b" :question/id #uuid "894f2b41-1597-5b67-ba7a-303a5bd60b9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-75780" :question/problem "![](images/36/36a99d1e792635936b3321144e89782e02cec2442a3cf2082939b3e78cdb69f4.png)\n\nWhat is the circumference of a circle with a radius of $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\pi }?$" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula $C=2\\pi r$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =2\\pi r \\\\  & =2\\pi \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\pi } \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0469b6c2-12d3-5657-beba-74f2906ede0b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0469b6c2-12d3-5657-beba-74f2906ede0b" :answer-field/id #uuid "0469b6c2-12d3-5657-beba-74f2906ede0b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-500407e2-57ff-5057-849c-279e291b15b3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2ec50246-36cb-5b2f-ac97-85bc18547680" "answer-f2aff979-41de-5a44-943f-bb761aa78442" "answer-500407e2-57ff-5057-849c-279e291b15b3" "answer-a03994e5-f125-58f0-801a-90620aaf2fda" "answer-34ff3527-1f9d-5220-b166-2afcaf2ec1e3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ec50246-36cb-5b2f-ac97-85bc18547680" :answer/id #uuid "2ec50246-36cb-5b2f-ac97-85bc18547680" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2aff979-41de-5a44-943f-bb761aa78442" :answer/id #uuid "f2aff979-41de-5a44-943f-bb761aa78442" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-500407e2-57ff-5057-849c-279e291b15b3" :answer/id #uuid "500407e2-57ff-5057-849c-279e291b15b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a03994e5-f125-58f0-801a-90620aaf2fda" :answer/id #uuid "a03994e5-f125-58f0-801a-90620aaf2fda" :answer