" :step/id #uuid "caa39b9e-dedd-5c18-9ea4-fda15a8732cf" :step/content "question-b42f766f-91bf-5b16-b807-3079a315696b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186086190 :answer-field/choices 17592186086192] [:db/retract 17592186086190 :answer-field/choices 17592186086193] [:db/retract 17592186086190 :answer-field/choices 17592186086194] [:db/retract 17592186086190 :answer-field/choices 17592186086195] [:db/retract 17592186086190 :answer-field/choices 17592186086191] {:db/id 17592186088256 :question/problem "Given that $-4{e}^{z}+7=5,$ then $z=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4{e}^{z}+7 & =5 \\\\ -4{e}^{z} & =-2 \\\\ {e}^{z} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{z} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{z}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ z & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $z=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186086190 :answer-field/correct "answer-ea5b3a18-587d-588e-a8f2-045924faba19" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5a966bea-c2c7-552f-8b5b-fa831cc51613" "answer-ea5b3a18-587d-588e-a8f2-045924faba19" "answer-e83c4852-1306-5f2d-9931-2c55058c46e3" "answer-83d81e6a-97cd-5d70-bf86-f4147a265d74" "answer-8f83f208-59ad-53c2-b961-74a5502985a2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a966bea-c2c7-552f-8b5b-fa831cc51613" :answer/id #uuid "5a966bea-c2c7-552f-8b5b-fa831cc51613" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea5b3a18-587d-588e-a8f2-045924faba19" :answer/id #uuid "ea5b3a18-587d-588e-a8f2-045924faba19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e83c4852-1306-5f2d-9931-2c55058c46e3" :answer/id #uuid "e83c4852-1306-5f2d-9931-2c55058c46e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83d81e6a-97cd-5d70-bf86-f4147a265d74" :answer/id #uuid "83d81e6a-97cd-5d70-bf86-f4147a265d74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f83f208-59ad-53c2-b961-74a5502985a2" :answer/id #uuid "8f83f208-59ad-53c2-b961-74a5502985a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087690 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4010032d-a265-55ab-a980-12aa209eef4e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-4010032d-a265-55ab-a980-12aa209eef4e" :question/id #uuid "4010032d-a265-55ab-a980-12aa209eef4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-100285" :question/problem "Find the solution to the equation ${e}^{8x}=\\sqrt{5}$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, we take $ln$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{8x} & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{8x}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{5}) \\\\ 8x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({5}^{1/2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule to the right-hand side and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx≈0.101\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e976916e-93a3-584d-9937-d0ffaf77228b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e976916e-93a3-584d-9937-d0ffaf77228b" :answer-field/id #uuid "e976916e-93a3-584d-9937-d0ffaf77228b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answe